{"type":"message","id":"b0a84118","parentId":"990ff565","timestamp":"2026-05-21T12:47:41.175Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"GET requests with X-API-Key header work but POST requests with the same header get Unauthorized. Let me try different approaches - maybe the POST needs Bearer token but GET needs X-API-Key, or vice versa. Or maybe the POST endpoint has different auth requirements.\n\nActually, looking at the previous successful GET with `X-API-Key`, maybe the POST requires `Authorization: Bearer` but we tried that and got Unauthorized. \n\nLet me try a few more combinations or check if the Cloudflare worker error 1101 is actually the real issue (Cloudflare Workers error 1101 is \"Worker thrown exception\" - so the worker itself is crashing, not an auth issue).\n\n\nThe error is definitely coming from Cloudflare Workers itself, not an authentication layer, so the server is receiving the requests but crashing when trying to process them. Let me test the endpoint with simpler payloads to see if that resolves the issue.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-c260bd41-4810-41e6-904f-763fb28cd6ce","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try POST with simpler payload to test if POST endpoint is working\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\": \"arbitration\", \"content\": \"test\"}'"},"partialArgs":"{\"command\":\"# Try POST with simpler payload to test if POST endpoint is working\\ncurl -s -X POST \\\"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\\\" \\\\\\n  -H \\\"X-API-Key: echo-a…key\\\" \\\\\\n  -H \\\"Content-Type: application/json\\\" \\\\\\n  -d '{\\\"threadId\\\": \\\"arbitration\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"test\\\"}'\"}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","