{"type":"message","id":"6b41e3ba","parentId":"1b0329b6","timestamp":"2026-05-21T12:48:29.076Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So GET with Bearer auth works for history but not for send. This is interesting. The GET endpoint works with `Authorization: Bearer` but POST /send returns 1101. Wait, earlier I got the history with `X-API-Key` header but POST failed with 1101...\n\nActually re-reading my first calls, the first GET attempts returned `Unauthorized` for both attempts, but then I got successful data when using `X-API-Key`. So:\n\n- GET /history: works with `X-API-Key`\n- GET /history: NOT work with `Authorization: Bearer`\n- POST /send: returns 1101 with `X-API-Key`\n\n\n- POST /send: returns `Unauthorized` with `Authorization: Bearer`\n\nSo I'm seeing different auth responses depending on which endpoint I'm hitting and which header I use. The 1101 error on the POST request is unusual though - that typically indicates a Cloudflare Workers issue with request body parsing, which could mean the Content-Type header or how the JSON payload is being formatted.\n\nWait, but I am setting the Content-Type header correctly to application/json. The problem might be that the /send endpoint expects a different authentication mechanism or the body format isn't quite right. Since both endpoints returned data for the GET request, the API key itself should be valid. Let me try the minimal payload approach again, or reconsider whether the Content-Type header might be conflicting with what the server actually expects - in some Worker configurations, having Content-Type can trigger body parsing before the request is fully validated. The 1101 error from Cloudflare Workers indicates the request body couldn't be parsed, which suggests the JSON structure might be malformed. But the JSON is properly formatted in my request, so there could be a character encoding issue or the server is rejecting the content for another reason. Let me try simplifying the request payload to see if that resolves the parsing error.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-24ac1a83-418d-45ea-a2d4-548986682e8a","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Check if it's a body size/content issue - try minimal\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d \"{\\\"threadId\\\":\\\"arbitration\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"heartbeat test\\\"}\""},"partialArgs":"{\"command\":\"# Check if it's a body size/content issue - try minimal\\ncurl -s -X POST \\\"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\\\" \\\\\\n  -H \\\"X-API-Key: echo-a…key\\\" \\\\\\n  -H \\\"Content-Type: application/json\\\" \\\\\\n  -d \\\"{\\\\\\\"threadId\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"arbitration\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"content\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"heartbeat test\\\\\\\"}\\\"\"}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":100,"output":491,"cacheRead":19840,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":20431,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779367695477,"responseId":"chatcmpl-e784ef83-516a-4f78-83a6-c8814ffc262a"}}
