{"type":"message","id":"81a4101b","parentId":"9772c714","timestamp":"2026-05-21T12:48:34.817Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The POST endpoint returns \"error code: 1101\" which seems like a Workers-specific error, while GET works with X-API-Key. The 1101 error from Cloudflare Workers typically means \"The request URI is malformed\" or could be a routing issue.\n\nLet me check the API endpoint path. Maybe it's `/api/send` instead of `/send`. But actually, the GET requests worked fine with the current URL structure, so it should be the same for POST.\n\nActually wait - Cloudflare Workers error 1101 is \"Script threw exception\" or could be a fetch assertion error. But the message just shows \"error code: 1101\" which is a bit unusual.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-01f434fe-0697-4c7a-ad94-435e541381d8","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try with trailing slash and check other path variations\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send/\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\": \"arbitration\", \"content\": \"test\"}'"},"partialArgs":"{\"command\":\"# Try with trailing slash and check other path variations\\ncurl -s -X POST \\\"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send/\\\" \\\\\\n  -H \\\"X-API-Key: echo-a…key\\\" \\\\\\n  -H \\\"Content-Type: application/json\\\" \\\\\\n  -d '{\\\"threadId\\\": \\\"arbitration\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"test\\\"}'\"}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":19971,"output":245,"cacheRead":96,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":20312,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779367709287,"responseId":"chatcmpl-ee2b9ab8-d297-4586-be3f-f571e153486b"}}
